            <ArticleTitle>An atypical presentation of an acute neurological illness: acute motor axonal neuropathy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>29-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pain is a common symptom amongst patients presenting to the Acute Medical Unit, with an extensive differential diagnosis. We present the case of a patient with back and lower limb pain where the diagnosis of an atypical form of Guillain-Barre Syndrome (GBS) was made. Acute physicians must be vigilant to the less common presentations of GBS and the variations from the &quot;classical&quot; presentation of ascending flaccid paralysis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
